 # Verify queued custom messages after abort are in active context
 
-
+Problem 3: messages may not render in main chat after queued messages exist and the blocking agent turn is aborted. Need distinguish UI bug vs data/context loss. Once a custom message emits message_start/message_end and persists as custom_message on the active branch, buildSessionContext should include it later. But source shows a real loss risk: sendCustomMessage while streaming queues a role custom object directly into core agent.steer/followUp and does not mirror it into AgentSession string queues; clearQueue/abort clears core queues and only restores mirrored string queues. A queued custom Chorus/Tattler message that has not drained can be silently dropped before persistence. Verify by reproducing mid-turn queue + abort and checking JSONL, active branch, and buildSessionContext.
